on_slug":"marise-payne","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mark Bishop","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10048","person_slug":"mark-bishop","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michael Forshaw","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10235","person_slug":"michael-forshaw","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mitch Fifield","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10224","person_slug":"mitch-fifield","vote":"no"},{"name":"Natasha Stott Despoja","party":"Australian Democrats","person_id":"tvfy_10613","person_slug":"natasha-stott-despoja","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick Sherry","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10576","person_slug":"nick-sherry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Paul Calvert","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10091","person_slug":"paul-calvert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Penny Wong","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10678","person_slug":"penny-wong","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Robert Ray","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10531","person_slug":"robert-ray","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ross Lightfoot","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10389","person_slug":"ross-lightfoot","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ruth Webber","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10662","person_slug":"ruth-webber","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Bill 2006 - In Committee - Definition of financing of terrorism","noes":44,"question":"The majority voted against an [amendment](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2006-12-07.138.1) introduced by Greens Senator [Kerry Nettle](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Kerry_Nettle&mpc=Senate&house=senate), which means that it was rejected. The amendment was: \"_(1) Clause 5, page 19 (lines 9 to 18), omit “:” and paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition of financing of terrorism, substitute “an offence under Division 103 of the Criminal Code”._\" Senator Nettle explained that this amendment \"seeks to narrow the definition of ‘financing terrorism’ that is used in the legislation\".(Read Senator Nettle's full explanation of her amendment and the related debate [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2006-12-07.132.1), after 5:16 pm. ) _Background to the bill_ This bill was introduced with the [Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Bill 2006](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:%22legislation/billhome/r2655%22). Its aim is to address the issue of money laundering in Australia and the potential threat to national security posed by the financing of terrorism.(Find out more about the bill, including its explanatory memorandum, [here](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/R2654). More information is available in the [bills digest](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/download/legislation/billsdgs/JGML6/upload_binary/jgml64.pdf;fileType=application%2Fpdf#search=%22r2654%22) (145 KB).) References","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1240","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2006-12-07/9"}
